{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T03:58:12.469Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0efcf6fa5f6489abf1ec4ce5","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.312","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T03:58:12.469Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"CodeRabbit round on 0a9a36c (4 minor), fixed by hand. (1) Git discovery validates only the .git marker, so standalone trackers below symlinked ancestors (macOS /var, linked /home) are no longer refused; a linked marker is still rl_state_path_invalid. The new checkpoint-artifacts test fails on revert. The durable-loop alias launch now resolves to the same shared authority (exit 0), and the second worktree still gets loop_launch_elsewhere. (2) Checkpoint-producing entry points (improver run, prefix meta recipes, prefix process fits) refuse checkpoint_storage_unsupported before any reservation, lease or receipt; the new mutation-preflight test fails when each of the three preflights is reverted separately. README documents the restriction. (3) The two sequential-evaluation tests start try right after setting PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS. (4) Card export and replay share citationOrder (UTF-8 bytes). It is unreachable today: native IDs are lowercase [a-z0-9-], pm rejects é and _, and 200k fuzzed pairs give identical code-unit and collation order. Unified to remove the latent mismatch. Suites: mutation-preflight + checkpoint-artifacts 44/44, policy-card replay 4/4, durable-loop alias 1/1; check (0 clones), docstring 499, lint, changelog pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T03:58:12.469Z"}],"before_hash":"284d25e437bfdbf540be2d4535fb56b2eb31e66136153f4b6